      "title": "Faculty Orientation Resources",
      "description": "Faculty Orientation Resources - Vice Provost Academic Planning Policy and Faculty APPF - Western University Skip to Content Faculty / Staff Search First Name Last Name or Department / Unit Search Search String Libraries Maps Parking Directory Websites A - Z Events WebMail OWL Brightspace Student Services WesternU.ca Office of the Vice-Provost (Academic Planning, Policy, and Faculty) and Office of Faculty Relations Office of the Vice-Provost (APP&F) and Office of Faculty Relations Popular Links Popular Links Directory Mail OWL Brightspace Student Services Websites A - Z Events Libraries Maps Parking WesternU Academic Planning Vice-Provost Interdisciplinary Development Initiatives Distinguished University Professorships (DUP) Award Faculty Scholar Award Faculty Relations Faculty (UWOFA) Clinical Faculty Librarians and Archivists Administrator Tools (Intranet - Secure LOGIN) Recruitment & Onboarding Hiring Resources Immigration Family Support Relocation Preparing for Leaves Faculty Orientation Resources Canada Research Chairs Canada Research Chairs Program - Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Public Accountability and Transparency Requirements Canada Research Chairs Program - Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Action Plan Academic Careers Faculty (UWOFA) Clinical Faculty Librarians / Archivists Research Chairs Equity, Diversity and Inclusion MENU Academic Planning Faculty Relations Recruitment & Onboarding Canada Research Chairs Academic Careers Home Recruitment & Onboarding Faculty Orientation Resources Recruitment Hiring Resources Immigration Family Support Relocation Preparing for Leaves Faculty Orientation Resources Contact Us Margaret McGlynn Professor Vice-Provost (Academic Planning, Policy & Faculty) 519-850-2900 mmcglyn@uwo.ca Geoff Wild, Professor Associate Vice-Provost (Academic Planning, Policy & Faculty) 519-661-2111 gwild@uwo.ca Heather Skilling Administrative Assistant 519-850-2900 hskillin@uwo.ca Margaret Poirier Senior Analyst 519-661-2111 (81150) mpoiri@uwo.ca Julie Watson Records Management Coordinator 519-661-2111 (84457) jwatson8@uwo.ca Faculty Orientation Resources This tool is a dynamic page designed to provide information to new faculty members and librarians.  This page consists of administrative information that individuals may require at some point during their academic year. Academic Policies for Faculty and Librarians Western's Secretariats' Office lists all of the policies and procedures approved by the Board of Governors for all Western employees.  Faculty and Staff will want to familiarize themselves to these policies as they oversee the govenance of Western. University Secretariat Setting up Essential University Resources Activate your Western Identity :  All personnel are required to activate their western identification and to so, you will need your Western ID number provided to you by your departmental administrator. Western ID Card :  All personnel are required to have a Western Identification card.  This card is essential for building access during off hours.  It may also be used for Western's meal plan and parking access. My HR : This portal is administered by Western's Human Resources and you will your username and password to access it.  This portal allows you to access pay information, personal information, benefits and T4 receipts. Health and Safety Training : All Western employees are required to complete mandatory work place modules.  Additional modules may be required for positions who are in a lab setting. IT Resources : Find information on Western's Brightspace, Helpdesk, Teams and other Western Technology Resources. Teaching at Western The Centre for Teaching and Learning provides support to new and current faculty members to acheive their teaching objectives.  Some preliminary resources available to new faculty: OWL Brightspace Learning Modules Centre for Teaching and Learning Programs Teaching Resources for Faculty E-learning Curriculum Development Research at Western Western University ranks as one of Canada’s top research-intensive universities. From fundamental to applied discovery and other scholarly activities, its scholars advance knowledge that provides tangible benefits for the economic, social, health and cultural development of citizens in London, in Canada and around the world. Extensive resources for Western researchers may be located on the Western Research Website including the following: Funding Opportunities Proposal Support Human Ethics Commercialize IP Awards and Distinctions Contact Information Important information on Budgeting and Spending Research Funds may be found on Western's Procurement Website: Research Finance Financial Information Navigating your way through your first year at Western can be difficult, specifically for some of the routine administrative tasks.  This is not an exhaustive list, but highlights some helpful links of what you may look for over the year in respect to finances. Procurement of goods related to Research Professional Expense Reimbursement Travel and Expense Reimbursement Benefit Claims Travel Coverage Outside of Canada/Ontario Collective Agreements The University of Western Ontario Faculty Association represents full-time professors of the University (other than clinical faculty) and also part-time faculty with duties equivalent to teaching at least 0.5 degree credit course in each of 2 of the last 3 fiscal years. The University of Western Ontario Faculty Agreement (UWOFA) UWOFA-LA represents those employees of the University performing the work of librarians and archivists. Librarians and Archivists Collective Agreement Wellness Health and wellness supports are available to all Western employees. As part of Western's employee benefits package, there is an Employee Assistance Program (EAP) provided by TELUS Health. Western University has an Employee and Family Health Clinic open to current faculty members and their family members.  New Faculty members must sign up for this clinic.  Information on the clinic including registration and elibibility information may be found here . Additional Resources Academic Staff Orientation Guide Academic Staff Administrative Checklist Presentations and Resource Materials from Orientation Day New Faculty Orientation Agenda 2024 Faculty Orientation - Center for Teaching and Learning Overview Faculty Orientation- Table Topics in Teaching Faculty Orientation- Registrar Faculty Orientation- Student Demographics Faculty Orientation - Wellness Faculty Orientation- Research Faculty Orientation - Research Primer aves, etc. Recruitment Hiring Resources Immigration Family Support Relocation Preparing for Leaves Faculty Orientation Resources © 1878 - 2026 Western University Vice-Provost (Academic Planning, Policy & Faculty) International and Graduate Affairs Building, Suite ON70, Lower Level London, Ontario, Canada, N6A 3K7 Tel: 519.850.2900 ofrweb@uwo.ca Privacy | Web Standards | Terms of Use | Accessibility Key Topics: Academic Planning Faculty Relations Recruitment & Onboarding Canada Research Chairs Academic Careers"
    },
